  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Task: The set `[1, 2, 3, ..., n]` includes a total of `n!` unique permutations.\n\nBy listing and labeling all of the permutations in order, we get the following sequence for `n = 3`:\n\n1. `\"123\"`\n2. `\"132\"`\n3. `\"213\"`\n4. `\"231\"`\n5. `\"312\"`\n6. `\"321\"`\n\nYou receive `n` and `k`, output the `kth` permutation sequence.",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= n <= 9",
      "1 <= k <= n!"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
    "notes": [],
